E("es-u2-214-q02",2,["EA12.2.14"],2,"var",varset([function(){return mcq("Earth is about 4.6 billion years old, and the Phanerozoic eon began about 541 million years ago. Approximately what percentage of Earth's history does Precambrian time represent?","about 88 percent",["about 12 percent","about 50 percent","about 65 percent"],"Precambrian time spans 4.6 billion minus 0.541 billion, about 4.06 billion years. 4.06 / 4.6 is about 0.88, so Precambrian time is about 88 percent of Earth history. The 12 percent figure is the Phanerozoic share.",{});}]),["Subtract, then divide by Earth's total age."]);

/* ----- EA12.2.15: The Phanerozoic eon represents the emergence of complex life forms ----- */
E("es-u2-215-q01",2,["EA12.2.15"],1,"var",varset([function(){return mcq("The name Phanerozoic means 'visible life'. Why is it an appropriate name for the current eon?","Its rocks preserve abundant fossils of large, complex life forms.",["It is the only eon in which living things existed on Earth.","Life became visible because eyes first evolved during the eon.","The eon's fossils are visible because they are all large dinosaurs."],"Phanerozoic rocks are full of obvious fossils of complex, multicellular organisms with shells, bones and other hard parts. Life existed long before, in the Precambrian, but it was mostly simple and microscopic, so it left a sparse fossil record.",{});}]),["Think about what shows up in the eon's rocks."]);
E("es-u2-215-q02",2,["EA12.2.15"],2,"var",varset([function(){return mcq("Which statement best distinguishes Phanerozoic time from Precambrian time?","Complex multicellular life emerges and diversifies through the Phanerozoic, while Precambrian life was dominated by simple, mostly single-celled organisms.",["Rocks of Phanerozoic age contain no fossils of any kind, because hard body parts had not yet evolved.","Precambrian time lasted only a few million years before complex life appeared at its end.","The Phanerozoic is another name for the Paleozoic era, the first era of complex life."],"The Phanerozoic is the eon of visible, complex life; the Precambrian, which came before it, was dominated by simple organisms. Watch the common mix-up: the Phanerozoic is an eon and contains the Paleozoic, Mesozoic and Cenozoic eras; it is not itself an era.",{});}]),["Eon versus era matters in one of these options."]);

